## Based on the standard .NET ignore set
## (https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Dotnet.gitignore),
## trimmed to what this repo can actually produce, plus the project-specific
## entries at the bottom.

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# .NET
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# MSBuild binary / structured log
*.binlog

# Test results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*
*.VisualState.xml

# Code coverage
CodeCoverage/

# dotenv
.env

# Editors and OS
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
~$*
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project-specific
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Note: the binary the MCP clients launch lives in bin/Debug/net8.0/ - Debug is
# the ONLY configuration this repo builds (see build.ps1) - and is ignored like
# any other build output, so a fresh clone must run build.ps1 once before the
# registered server can start. That is deliberate: there is exactly ONE compiled
# artifact, so nothing can drift out of sync.
#
# This note said bin/Release/net8.0/ until 2026-08-09. It was wrong, and it was
# the only place in the repo still pointing at Release - which is exactly how a
# second, stale artifact gets built by someone following the comment.

# Scratch output from AIXML round-trips
*.aixml
schema.txt

# Claude Code settings: the SHARED file is part of the repo on purpose - it
# allow-lists the read-only lvai_* tools so they run without a prompt
# (README section 6). Only the per-machine overrides are ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python build artifacts (scripts/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Plugin staging directories: the release workflow fills plugin/bin/ (the published
# exe) and plugin/scripts/ (a copy of the repo's scripts/) at pack time. They are build
# output and must never be committed. plugin/bin/ is already covered by [Bb]in/ above;
# the entries here are anchored with a leading slash so they only match under plugin/ and
# leave the repository's own top-level scripts/ tracked.
/plugin/bin/
/plugin/scripts/

# Release-workflow working directories and the packed asset, in case the pack steps are run
# locally. In CI these live only in the ephemeral runner workspace.
/staging/
/publish/
/labview-mcp.zip
